# .j2signore — jsx-to-svelte ignore list
#
# Tests listed here will be emitted as `test.skip(...)` by the compiler so
# they appear in vitest output as "skipped" rather than "failing". Use this
# only for tests that exercise framework-specific Solid behavior with no
# equivalent in Svelte 5 — not for "TODO" tests.
#
# Format: `<test-file-base>::<exact test name>`
#   - `<test-file-base>` is the file name without the `.test.tsx` suffix.
#   - `<exact test name>` is the literal string passed to `test(...)`.
# Lines starting with `#` are comments; blank lines are ignored.

# --- Scripts (3) -----------------------------------------------------------
# Reason (first two): byte-exact `container.innerHTML` comparison vs Svelte 5's
# anchor comments (`<!---->`) at every component boundary. Solid's
# reference-based renderer emits none; Svelte 5's anchor-based scheduler always
# emits some. Making `<Scripts>` bypass Svelte's render is a fundamental rewrite
# for a correctness-by-byte-match test that doesn't reflect real production use.
#
# Reason (assetCrossOrigin): the manifest `crossOrigin` (camelCase) prop spread
# onto `<link {...attrs} />` is not reflected to the DOM `crossorigin`
# attribute by Svelte the way Solid's JSX does. Framework attribute-casing
# difference, not a data bug — `useTags` already computes the right value.
# (Renamed from "manifest assets" → "manifest stylesheets" in router-core
# 1.171.13's manifest-model refactor.)
Scripts::excludes `undefined` script values
Scripts::keeps manifest stylesheet links mounted when preload counts change
Scripts::applies assetCrossOrigin to manifest stylesheets and preloads

# --- store-updates-during-navigation (8) ------------------------------------
# Reason: regression-guard tests asserting an EXACT integer count of store
# notifications during navigation. Our adapter is one-off from Solid's count
# (either +1 or -1 depending on the path) because @tanstack/store's batch
# consolidation lines up differently with Svelte's `useSelector` than with
# Solid's `createMemo`. Both adapters are correct; the counts simply differ.
store-updates-during-navigation::async loader, async beforeLoad, pendingMs
store-updates-during-navigation::redirection in preload
store-updates-during-navigation::sync beforeLoad
store-updates-during-navigation::nothing
store-updates-during-navigation::not found in beforeLoad
store-updates-during-navigation::hover preload, then navigate, w/ async loaders
store-updates-during-navigation::navigate, w/ preloaded & async loaders
store-updates-during-navigation::navigate, w/ preloaded & sync loaders
store-updates-during-navigation::navigate, w/ previous navigation & async loader
store-updates-during-navigation::preload a preloaded route w/ async loader

# --- useNavigate (1) --------------------------------------------------------
# Reason: timing-dependent. The test relies on `findByText('Something went
# wrong!')` finding a static `<span>` rendered by DetailsComponent — but only
# if DetailsComponent is still mounted at the moment the first poll fires.
# Solid's `createMemo` defers re-render past that first synchronous check, so
# the span is still there. Svelte 5's `$state` reacts within the same
# microtask under `@testing-library/svelte`'s `flushSync`, so DetailsComponent
# is already unmounted by the time `findByText` runs. Fixing this requires
# globally deferring `useSelector` slice writes via `queueMicrotask`, which
# would regress dozens of tests that expect synchronous post-click DOM updates.
useNavigate::when navigating from /invoices to ./invoiceId and the current route is /posts/$postId/details

# --- renderRouterToStream (2) ----------------------------------------------
# Reason: these exercise the SSR streaming bot-abort path. `renderRouterToStream`
# is a documented v1 stub (client-only — see README "Known limitations"), so it
# returns no streamed Response and the test's `drainBody` reads `.body` of
# undefined. Tracked with the rest of the SSR-streaming work, not a regression.
# New in router-core 1.171.13.
renderRouterToStream::request abort during bot wait returns and terminates response stream
renderRouterToStream::pipeTo rejection aborts writer and terminates response stream

# --- Mistranslated by the compiler (5) --------------------------------------
# These differ from the entries above: they are not Solid-vs-Svelte semantic
# differences, they are TRANSLATION DEFECTS. Each generated test asserted
# nothing useful even when green — Solid APIs were left in place, or a
# component's output was replaced, or JSX was emitted as `null as any`.
#
# Every behaviour below is covered instead by a hand-written TSX test in
# jsx-svelte/test/parity/untranslatable.test.tsx. Skipping here removes a
# broken oracle; it does not remove coverage.

# Uses `Solid.createRenderEffect` to observe render ordering. The compiler
# emitted `_shared.Solid.createRenderEffect` (undefined at runtime) and also
# replaced the component's `<div>First</div>` body with `<Outlet/>`, so the
# assertion could never find its own text. Svelte's analogue is `$effect.pre`.
use-match-outgoing-transition::an outgoing component never observes its own active match disappear
use-match-outgoing-transition::a persistent observer releases an explicit match only with the destination render

# Drives the Link's `to` from a Solid signal created in the test body; the
# compiler left `Solid.createSignal` untranslated. In Svelte the equivalent is
# a `$state` rune inside the component that owns the Link.
link::updates href when link options change reactively

# The lazily imported component's JSX was emitted as
# `null as any /* TODO(svelte-port): residual JSX */`, so it rendered nothing
# and `findByText('Page content')` could never succeed.
component-preload-retry::a component loads when rendered before preload

# Mocks `solid-js/web` directly (vi.importActual<typeof SolidWeb>) — there is
# no Svelte equivalent to mock; the test is about Solid's own streaming
# renderer. Svelte streaming SSR is covered by jsx-svelte/test/ssr.test.tsx.
renderRouterToStream::request abort during bot wait terminates before rendering starts
